From 9bac2bdac6c4c168cdab0513e31b6db2e59d59c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:40:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: error reporting without cost on success

The devices only write the statistics of the behaviours and the statuses
of the material properties when an event occurs at a point (failure,
unreliable result, decrease of the time step scaling factor, bound
violated, invalid result).

Behaviours and models (data structures version 2):
- index of the first point where the computations failed, in the
  statistics and in the output status, independent of the order of the
  computations (atomic minimum or reduction, all backends);
- CUDA and HIP: warps without event skip the reductions (vote);
- synchronous CUDA, HIP and SYCL computations: the statistics are held by
  a block of managed or shared memory, initialized and read by the host,
  instead of a device allocation, copies and a deallocation per call.

Material properties: the statuses of the bounds checks are held by the
same kind of blocks on all the backends, instead of an allocation per
call. The CUDA and HIP backends synchronize the stream instead of the
device.

The blocks are allocated at the first call on a device and reused
(mfront::generic_parallel::StatusBlockPool), one block per running call.

The comparison program checks the index of the first failure. The HIP
test of the material properties no longer assumes that the memory given
by hipMallocManaged is zeroed.
